---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// The essay is the landing page and the sky is its backdrop (M5). Headings come from the same
// chapters the asterisms are built from, so a chapter can never be lit with no words under it, or
// read with no figure behind it.
const { chapters } = (await getEntry('topology', 'thales'))!.data;
const body: Record<string, string[]> = {
  warehouse: [
    'When I was 14 the family computer had a hardware failure, so I scrapped together a new one. Rather than install Windows Vista I chose a Debian distro called Crunchbang. Thus began a lifelong obsession with Linux and FOSS.',
    'I had no idea what I wanted to do when I grew up. It never occurred to me that this could be the job, or that I\'d be any good at it.',
  ],
  philosophy: [
    'In high school I got sick. In high school I spent more time in bed than in class. I was scouring StackOverflow for help with Makefiles, installing Gentoo, learning Python. I graduated on time at 17 anyway, thanks to summer school.',
    'I worked in factories and warehouses for a few years, then enrolled at UNLV to study one of my other passions, philosophy. In school I studied logic and systems of thinking, the history of ideas and the nature of intelligence. The analytical skills I learned then I use now more than ever.',
  ],
  'vet-med': [
    'Junior year I took a job at a veterinary hospital, and ended up staying through the pandemic. After a few years and a few bites I decided enough was enough. I started studying for the CompTIA A+ on my lunch breaks, got the certification, and aggressively pursued help desk jobs until Circa took a chance on me.',
  ],
  'casino-it': [
    'At Circa I was promptly promoted to Desktop Support Specialist. About a year later, Sysadmin. About a year after that, I let slip that I run a sophisticated Kubernetes cluster in my homelab, and not long after that, Cloud Engineer.',
    'I’ve never liked going to work, or at least I thought. I always wanted to be at home tinkering and it took a long time to realize the two aren’t mutually exclusive. I didn’t hate going to work; I hated having to stop tinkering.',
  ],
};
---
<Base bodyClass="landing">
  <h1>Jason Harker</h1>
  <p class="dek">Cloud engineer in Las Vegas. This is how I got here.</p>
  <article class="essay">
    {chapters.map((chapter) => (
      <section class="prose" data-chapter={chapter.id}>
        {(body[chapter.id] ?? []).map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
      </section>
    ))}
  </article>
</Base>
